{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which of the following is true about Legendre polynomials?", "option1": "They are orthogonal over [−1,1] with weight w(x)=1.", "option2": "They satisfy a Sturm–Liouville problem.", "option3": "They appear in solutions of Laplace’s equation in spherical coordinates.", "option4": "All of the above", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_HMCJrAy.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"503\" height=\"571\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Bessel functions arise as eigenfunctions of:", "option1": "Laplace’s equation in cylindrical coordinates", "option2": "Heat equation in Cartesian coordinates", "option3": "Wave equation in Cartesian coordinates", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Separation of variables in cylindrical systems leads to Bessel’s equation for the radial part.</p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which of the following best explains why Bessel functions are important in wave propagation?", "option1": "They approximate sinusoidal motion", "option2": "They represent standing waves in circular/elliptical geometries", "option3": "They only apply to 1D vibrations", "option4": "They remove damping effects", "answer": "0", "exp": "Bessel functions describe radial oscillations in 2D/3D geometries (circular membranes, cylindrical pipes, antennas, waveguides)."}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which of the following is NOT an application of Fourier series?", "option1": "Solving the heat equation", "option2": "Signal processing and communication", "option3": "Image compression (JPEG)", "option4": "Finding eigenvalues of Legendre equation", "answer": "4", "exp": "Fourier series is widely used in PDEs (heat, wave, Laplace equations), signal &amp; image processing, and data compression.<br />But Legendre&rsquo;s equation is solved by Legendre polynomials, not Fourier series."}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) If f(x) is an odd function, then its Fourier series contains:", "option1": "Only cosine terms", "option2": "Only sine terms", "option3": "Both sine and cosine terms", "option4": "Only the constant term", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_QA8Qcrp.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1063\" height=\"313\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which of the following is a direct consequence of Riemann’s theorem?", "option1": "Parseval’s identity always holds", "option2": "Fourier series converges uniformly for all functions", "option3": "a<sub>n</sub>​,b<sub>n</sub> ​→ 0 as n → ∞", "option4": "f(x) must be even", "answer": "3", "exp": "<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_uLalESZ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"796\" height=\"76\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Which of the following functions does NOT satisfy the condition for Riemann’s theorem?", "option1": "A piecewise continuous function", "option2": "A bounded function", "option3": "A function with infinite discontinuities in [- π, π]", "option4": "A function defined on [- π, π]", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><br />The theorem requires the function to be piecewise continuous (finite discontinuities allowed). If there are infinitely many discontinuities, the condition fails.</p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Using Rodrigue's Formula \r\nP<sub>1</sub>(x) = ?", "option1": "1", "option2": "x", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_ushbJ6l.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"129\" height=\"58\" />", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "0", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_ushbJ6l.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"129\" height=\"58\" /><br /><br /><br />Using All kind of Formula, P<sub>1</sub>(x) is always x."}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_9BGxxWo.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"335\" height=\"97\" />", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_SzAauwA.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"222\" height=\"43\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-24_025312588.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"222\" height=\"43\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-24_025443076.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"222\" height=\"43\" />", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-24_025532238.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"396\" height=\"37\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-24_025556336.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"405\" height=\"64\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) A function f(x) with period 2π can be expressed as:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_5A7B5hb.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"428\" height=\"44\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_wZsS8xE.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"428\" height=\"44\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_Mdtv6wy.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"428\" height=\"44\" />", "option4": "Both B and C", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_233002752.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"376\" height=\"174\" /></p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) The Fourier series was originally developed by Joseph Fourier to solve problems related to:", "option1": "Vibrations of strings", "option2": "Heat conduction", "option3": "Electrical circuits", "option4": "Quantum mechanics", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Fourier first introduced the Fourier series in his study of the heat equation in 1822. Later, it was applied in many other fields like vibrations, circuits, and physics.</p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Express J<sub>1</sub>(x) in terms of J<sub>0​</sub>(x) and J<sub>2</sub>(x).", "option1": "J<sub>1</sub>​(x) = [(J<sub>0​</sub>(x) - J<sub>2</sub>​(x)]/2", "option2": "J<sub>1</sub>​(x) = [(J<sub>0</sub>​(x) - J<sub>2</sub>​(x)]", "option3": "J<sub>1​</sub>(x) = [(J<sub>0</sub>​(x) + J<sub>2</sub>​(x)]/2", "option4": "J<sub>1</sub>​(x) = [(J<sub>0</sub>​(x) + J<sub>2​</sub>(x)]", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-24_023012836.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"284\" height=\"35\" /><br />​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-24_023117327.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"310\" height=\"56\" /></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_gvMKx3y.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"322\" height=\"143\" />", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_Ux8gdLm.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"214\" height=\"69\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_3KPmg3n.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"214\" height=\"69\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/4_PL6BhqM.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"214\" height=\"69\" />", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_194206251.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"276\" height=\"49\" /><br />​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_194632024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"333\" height=\"85\" /></p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) The periodic square wave function f(x) defined in (- &pi;, &pi;) as&nbsp;<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_YEe8Llp.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"352\" height=\"99\" /> has Fourier expansion involving:", "option1": "Only cosine term", "option2": "Only sine terms", "option3": "Both sine and cosine terms", "option4": "Constant term only", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-21_203926942.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"615\" height=\"127\" /></p>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_JKftV5g.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"667\" height=\"119\" />", "option1": "2π", "option2": "0", "option3": "Divergent", "option4": "π<sup>2</sup>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><br />its integral tends to zero by Riemann&rsquo;s theorem <br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-21_052448515.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"257\" height=\"118\" /></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which one in true?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_5segyou.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"387\" height=\"56\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_TO1zw3Z.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"387\" height=\"56\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_4UdpbeU.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"387\" height=\"56\" />", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_193624005.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"361\" height=\"35\" /><br />​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_193743506.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"421\" height=\"75\" /></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_oEI34sB.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"266\" height=\"77\" />", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_gs8HZbB.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"159\" height=\"58\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_ob3Qlwg.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"159\" height=\"58\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/4_qymSnAz.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"159\" height=\"58\" />", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_192938694.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"302\" height=\"30\" /><br />​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_193013217.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"398\" height=\"68\" /></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which of the following derivative relations is correct for Legendre polynomials?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_4bqK84Q.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"430\" height=\"39\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_xuV9PrL.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"488\" height=\"36\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_KVsLMTm.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"418\" height=\"37\" />", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/4_9AsN1Kq.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"367\" height=\"39\" />", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-21_232734112.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"412\" height=\"66\" /></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Riemann’s theorem is most useful in proving which property of Fourier coefficients?", "option1": "&nbsp;a<sub>0</sub>=0 for odd functions", "option2": "Fourier coefficients are bounded by O(1/n)", "option3": "Fourier coefficients vanish at infinity", "option4": "Fourier series converges absolutely for every function", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>The theorem ensures that as n→∞, a<sub>n</sub>→0and b<sub>n</sub>→0, which is essential for Fourier series representation.</p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which of the following functions does NOT satisfy Dirichlet’s conditions in (- π, π)?", "option1": "f(x) = sin(x)", "option2": "f(x) =।x।", "option3": "f(x) = tan(x)", "option4": "f(x) = x<sup>2</sup>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-21_112617229.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"503\" height=\"76\" /></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which of the following is the differential equation satisfied by the modified Bessel function I<sub>n</sub>​(x) ?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_AfC1Jj2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"366\" height=\"44\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_7Bx7CZT.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"389\" height=\"47\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_Th31IMh.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"370\" height=\"70\" />", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-22_095059025.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"335\" height=\"77\" /></p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) which one is correct?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_PCMZi4z.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"323\" height=\"40\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_XREs0hP.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"307\" height=\"38\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_nsK5uJq.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"307\" height=\"36\" />", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/4_qoodhSz.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"307\" height=\"41\" />", "answer": "0", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-21_233532088.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"449\" height=\"62\" /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-21_233606663.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"376\" height=\"60\" /></p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Which of the following problems is most suitable for half-range Fourier expansion?", "option1": "&nbsp;A vibrating string fixed at both ends, displacement given in (0,L).", "option2": "Motion in free space without boundaries", "option3": "Probability distribution problems", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Half range Fourier expansions are widely used in vibrating string and heat conduction problems where functions are defined only on (0,L).</p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) If a function is not periodic, can its Fourier series representation exist?", "option1": "Yes, always", "option2": "No, never", "option3": "Yes, if it is extended periodically", "option4": "Only if it is discontinuous", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Fourier series require periodicity. A non-periodic function can still have a Fourier series if it is periodically extended outside the given interval.</p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which differential equation is satisfied by Legendre polynomials?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_DjcqNVo.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"342\" height=\"56\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_CYYebGs.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"54\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_eWh30RU.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"392\" height=\"53\" />", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/4_I3yo7Az.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"397\" height=\"47\" />", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-22_014322013.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"499\" height=\"68\" /></p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) J<sub>2</sub>(- x) = ?", "option1": "J<sub>- 2</sub>​(x)", "option2": "- J<sub>- 2</sub>​(x)", "option3": "- J<sub>2</sub>​(x)", "option4": "J<sub>2​</sub>(x)", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_191358831.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"42\" /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_191425236.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"390\" height=\"102\" /></p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Dirichlet’s conditions ensure that:", "option1": "The Fourier series always converges uniformly.", "option2": "&nbsp;The Fourier series always converges to the original function everywhere.", "option3": "The Fourier series converges pointwise to the function or to the average at discontinuities.", "option4": "The Fourier series does not converge.", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Dirichlet’s theorem guarantees pointwise convergence. At discontinuities, it converges to the average of left and right-hand limits. It does not guarantee uniform convergence.</p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) The normalization constant for J<sub>2</sub>(α<sub>m</sub>x) is:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_ndgKpM9.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"168\" height=\"65\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_Z3V20n4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"165\" height=\"63\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_5ab7OnB.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"142\" height=\"51\" />", "option4": "0", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_190149357.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"408\" height=\"98\" /></p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) If f(x) = x in [-π, π], then its Fourier series:", "option1": "Converges uniformly.", "option2": "&nbsp;Does not converge uniformly but converges pointwise.", "option3": "Diverges everywhere.", "option4": "Converges only at x=0.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><br />Here, f(&minus;&pi;)=&minus;&pi; and f(&pi;)=&pi;, which are not equal. Thus, the periodic extension introduces a jump discontinuity. The Fourier series converges pointwise everywhere except at the discontinuity, but not uniformly</p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Which of the following waves satisfies Dirichlet’s conditions?", "option1": "Square wave", "option2": "Triangular wave", "option3": "Sawtooth wave", "option4": "All of the above", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-21_112900212.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"441\" height=\"138\"></p>"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) For m &gt; p&nbsp;<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_o1LQEKV.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"401\" height=\"102\" />", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "∞", "option4": "None of These", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><br />​m&ne;p<br />​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_185947082.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"502\" height=\"42\" /></p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Which is the differential equation for modified Bessel functions In(x)?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_IMBF3hu.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"426\" height=\"50\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_sqSP3af.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"314\" height=\"41\" />", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_cGhPsPq.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"331\" height=\"46\" />", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "0", "exp": "<p><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-23_110607073.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"81\" /></p>"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_vm5xq6L.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"537\" height=\"78\" />", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_RNpaL8G.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"214\" height=\"98\" />", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_gCPFLSc.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"214\" height=\"98\" />", "option3": "<span id=\"mce_1_start\" style=\"overflow: hidden; line-height: 0px;\">sinx</span>", "option4": "<span id=\"mce_1_start\" style=\"overflow: hidden; line-height: 0px;\">cosx</span>", "answer": "1", "exp": ""}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_YAhGUSZ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"534\" height=\"160\" />", "option1": "2/7", "option2": "0", "option3": "7/2", "option4": "2/9", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_YAhGUSZ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"534\" height=\"160\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-22_011505316.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"341\" height=\"76\" /></p>"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) The standard form of Bessel’s differential equation of order n is:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-05104032355